depolarizationMap -- creates the depolarization map
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        depolarizationMap(R,S)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a polynomial ring
      * S, a polynomial ring in twice as many variables as R
  * Outputs:
      * a ring map S to R that depolarizes squarefree monomials

Description
===========

A method that returns the depolarization map of Gunturkun, Jeffries, and Sun.
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3];                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3,y_1..y_3];                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : depolarizationMap(R,S)                          |
|                                                     |
|o3 = map (R, S, {x , x , x , x  + 1, x  + 1, x  + 1})|
|                  1   2   3   1       2       3      |
|                                                     |
|o3 : RingMap R <-- S                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use depolarizationMap:
==============================

  * "depolarizationMap(Ring,Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note depolarizationMap: depolarizationMap, is a *note method
function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

