isCanonical -- determines whether a neural ideal is in canonical form
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isCanonical(I)
  * Inputs:
      * I, a neural ideal
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Polarized => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * Boolean

Description
===========

A method that determines whether a neural ideal is in canonical form.
Currently, it computes the canonical form and compares, so it may not be
accurate and is not quick.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3];        |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : I=ideal(x_1,x_2*(1-x_1));|
|                              |
|o2 : Ideal of R               |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : isCanonical(I)           |
|                              |
|o3 = false                    |
+------------------------------+

Ways to use isCanonical:
========================

  * "isCanonical(Ideal)"

