polarizedCanonicalForm -- computes the polarized canonical form
***************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        polarizedCanonicalForm(C,S) or polarizedCanonicalForm(C) or polarizedCanonicalForm(I,S)
  * Inputs:
      * C,a neural code or I, an ideal
      * S, a ring where the polarization will live
  * Outputs:
      * a List of squarefree monomials (in S if S is specified, else in
        polarizedRing(C)

Description
===========

A method that returns the polarized canonical form of a neural code or neural
ideal
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3,y_1..y_3];                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C=neuralCode({"000","100","110","101","001"});|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : polarizedCanonicalForm(C)                     |
|                                                   |
|o3 = {x y , x x }                                  |
|       2 1   2 3                                   |
|                                                   |
|o3 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : R=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3];          |
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : I=ideal(x_1,x_2*(1-x_1));  |
|                                |
|o5 : Ideal of R                 |
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : S=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3,y_1..y_3]; |
+--------------------------------+
|i7 : polarizedCanonicalForm(I,S)|
|                                |
|o7 = {x , x }                   |
|       1   2                    |
|                                |
|o7 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+

