polarizedCanonicalIdeal -- polarized ideal generated by the canonical form
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        polarizedCanonicalIdeal(C) or polarizedCanonicalIdeal(I,S)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a NeuralCode, or I, a squarefree pseudomonomial ideal
      * S a ring where the polarization will live
  * Outputs:
      * A squarefree monomial ideal, in polarizedRing(C) or in S.

Description
===========

A method that returns the ideal generated by the polarized canonical form of a
neural code or neural ideal.
+-------------------------------+
|i1 : C=neuralCode({"00","10"});|
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : polarizedCanonicalIdeal(C)|
|                               |
|o2 = ideal x                   |
|            2                  |
|                               |
|              ZZ               |
|o2 : Ideal of --[x ..y ]       |
|               2  1   2        |
+-------------------------------+
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : R=ZZ/2[x_1,x_2];            |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : I=ideal(x_1*x_2);           |
|                                 |
|o4 : Ideal of R                  |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : S=ZZ/2[x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2];    |
+---------------------------------+
|i6 : polarizedCanonicalIdeal(I,S)|
|                                 |
|o6 = ideal(x x )                 |
|            1 2                  |
|                                 |
|o6 : Ideal of S                  |
+---------------------------------+

