      * S, a ring with twice as many variables as ring(f), where the
        polarization will live
  * Outputs:
      * a squarefree monomial (in S if S is given)

Description
===========

A method which takes a pseudomonomial in a polynomial ring and replaces every
instance of (1-var) with a new variable. It is recommended that you specify the
ring in which the new monomial will live, see examples below.
+--------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3];          |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : f=x_1*(1-x_2);             |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : S=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3,y_1..y_3]; |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : polarizePseudomonomial(f,S)|
|                                |
|o4 = x y                        |
|      1 2                       |
|                                |
|o4 : S                          |
+--------------------------------+

