receptiveFieldRelation -- gives the receptive field relation corresponding ot a pseudomonomial
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        receptiveFieldRelation(f)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a squarefree pseudomonomial
  * Outputs:
      * a List of two Lists

Description
===========

A method which returns the receptive field relation corresponding to a
pseudomonomial. It returns it as a list containing two lists, such that the
intersection of the firing fields corresponding to the elements of the first
list is contained in the union of the firing fields corresponding to the
elements of the second list.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/2[x_1..x_3];        |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : f=x_1*(1-x_2)*(1-x_3);   |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : receptiveFieldRelation(f)|
|                              |
|o3 = {{1}, {2, 3}}            |
|                              |
|o3 : List                     |
+------------------------------+

Ways to use receptiveFieldRelation:
===================================

  * "receptiveFieldRelation(RingElement)"

